Subject: [PATCH] ctrl: an agent's renewed radios do not wait for its configured ones

After M2 a radio waits in topo_sync_pending, and the controller sends the
agent's Topology Query only when every radio of the agent is there. When only
some radios are renewed (their em_config timed out once, they were marked
misconfigured and AutoConfig Renew re-ran WSC for them alone), the radio that
stayed configured never comes back to topo_sync_pending: the renewed radios
wait for it until their em_config times out, are renewed again and wait again,
for ever. Each round drops their BSSes from the model and re-adds them, about
once a minute (seen on rdk-emosa-1001's wired extender, 1 Oct: its 2.4 and
5 GHz radios cycling, its 6 GHz radio configured).

Only a sibling still onboarding (before topo_sync_pending) holds the query
now; one past topology sync does not. The radio that sends the query is
elected among the radios waiting for it, since a configured sibling may be
executing another command.

Upstream-Status: Pending

--- a/src/em/config/em_configuration.cpp
+++ b/src/em/config/em_configuration.cpp
@@ -7220,7 +7220,11 @@
             if (ssid_mismatch_present == false)
             {
                 for (auto &em : em_radios) {
-                    if (em->get_state() != em_state_ctrl_topo_sync_pending) {
+                    // Only a sibling still onboarding (before topology sync) holds the
+                    // query. One already past it, because it finished earlier and only
+                    // this radio was renewed, must not: waiting for it times this radio's
+                    // em_config out, renews it and waits again, for ever.
+                    if (em->get_state() < em_state_ctrl_topo_sync_pending) {
                         em_printfout("radio %s is in state:%d, not in topo sync pending state, ignoring",
                             util::mac_to_string(em->get_radio_interface_mac()).c_str(), em->get_state());
                         em_radios.clear();
@@ -7234,8 +7238,11 @@
                 // can finish its orchestration before the last sibling reaches this state.
                 // Elect a radio whose state machine is actually still executing, otherwise
                 // no candidate can pass the old `this == em_radios.front()` gate.
+                // ... and among the radios waiting for this query: a sibling already
+                // past topology sync may be executing another command.
                 auto query_em = std::find_if(em_radios.begin(), em_radios.end(), [](em_t *radio) {
-                    return radio->get_orch_state() == em_orch_state_progress;
+                    return radio->get_state() == em_state_ctrl_topo_sync_pending &&
+                        radio->get_orch_state() == em_orch_state_progress;
                 });
                 if (query_em != em_radios.end() && this == *query_em) {
                     em_printfout("Sending the Topology query message to agent al_mac:%s on radio: %s",
